  "scriptId": "avg-05-missing-overlapping-and-partial-averages",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Missing, Overlapping and Partial Averages",
    "description": "Recover hidden observations from partial averages, overlapping groups and repeated middle values.",
    "teachingApproach": "Teach learners to convert every partial mean into a subtotal and to track exactly which observations belong to each subtotal. Progress from a single hidden middle value to remainders, overlapping first/last groups, overlapping time windows, pairwise averages, direct window subtraction, a data-sufficiency check and a capstone that combines partial totals with relative differences.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 32,
    "sourceScope": "Teach partial-average questions by converting every stated mean into a sum and marking which observations each subtotal contains. Cover a hidden middle value, an unmentioned remainder, overlapping first-k and last-k groups where one observation is counted twice, overlapping day/temperature windows, pairwise averages, and direct subtraction of overlapping windows. Include a data-sufficiency checkpoint showing that group means alone may not determine a combined mean without group sizes. End with a capstone that combines subset totals with relative differences among the remaining observations."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn the average questions where the real challenge is not division — it is knowing what has already been counted.\n\nWe will turn every average into a subtotal, then keep a close eye on overlaps.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Five numbers average 40, so their total is 200. The first two average 35, giving 70. The last two average 42, giving 84.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Only the middle number is missing from those two edge groups.\n\nMiddle = 200 − 70 − 84 = 46\n\nThe trick is to turn every partial average into the subtotal it describes.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
